VERSION 2 — Firm but Collegial
Subject: Checklist Controls — Mandatory Standards Reminder (Effective Immediately)
Team,
I want to address some concerns around how our daily and biweekly checklist controls are being
handled, and set clear expectations going forward.
WHAT WE NEED TO STOP
Some checklists are being submitted with generic comments ("checks performed", "yes/no") without the
controls actually being carried out. Exports are being attached without the underlying checks being
done. When validators flag issues, responses have been "I'll do it tomorrow" — which is not in line with
our procedures.
Supervisors hold us accountable to these checklists as audit evidence. We need to treat them
accordingly.
FOR PREPARERS — YOUR RESPONSIBILITIES THIS WEEK AND EVERY WEEK
• Start the day by reviewing that day's emails, then immediately begin the checklist controls. This is
your first priority, not an end-of-day task.
• Do not start controls at 6–7 PM and submit incomplete. If controls are not finished properly, they
need to be redone — not carried forward.
• After completing each check, send the relevant exports and screenshots (e.g. from Hobart) to your
validator by email as evidence. Comments alone will not be accepted.
FOR VALIDATORS — YOUR RESPONSIBILITIES
• Do not accept checklists based on trust alone. Confirm the preparer has completed all controls
with evidence.
• Review and validate between 7 PM and 8 PM each day.
• Watch for: unassigned emails, SRs unacknowledged for 10+ days, and any missing actions.
• If a check is incomplete or unsupported by evidence, reject it and ask the preparer to redo it before
you sign off.
